diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index bb50321..5960f7b 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- `format_stats` shows sizes in binary units (`bytes: 1.5 KiB`) and a new `average:` line; `LogStats` gains `average_record_bytes`.
 - Index entries store the offset relative to the segment's base offset in 4 bytes (8-byte entries), and the index is sparse: new `index_interval_bytes` option, default 4096.
 - Segment format version 2: the record length prefix is a varint instead of a 4-byte integer. Version 1 segments are refused.
 - `eventlog dump --from` defaults to the first offset still in the log.
diff --git a/docs/reference.md b/docs/reference.md
index 63412b1..992b5ab 100644
--- a/docs/reference.md
+++ b/docs/reference.md
@@ -68,9 +68,11 @@ Records follow the segment header back to back.
 
 `stats(directory)` reads the files without opening the log. `format_stats` prints one `name: value` line per field.
 
+`average_record_bytes` is the mean encoded record size: segment bytes minus the segment headers, divided by the record count, rounded to one decimal place, and `0.0` with no records. `format_stats` shows `bytes` in binary units, whole bytes below 1024 (`bytes: 512 B`) and one decimal place in KiB, MiB or GiB above (`bytes: 1.5 KiB`), followed directly by an `average: 41.2 B` line.
+
 | Field | Value | Meaning |
 |---|---|---|
-| `stats.fields` | `segments records keys tombstones bytes first_offset next_offset` | `LogStats` fields, in order. |
+| `stats.fields` | `segments records keys tombstones bytes average_record_bytes first_offset next_offset` | `LogStats` fields, in order. |
 | `stats.bytes` | `segment files` | Total size of segment files, headers included; index files are not counted. |
 | `stats.offsets_line` | `offsets: {first_offset}..{next_offset}` | How `format_stats` shows the two offset fields. |
 
